1
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:18,500
From zero to hero.

2
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:31,000
The Mask is a romance, comedy, crime film directed by Chuck Russell.

3
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:43,500
Stanley, a meek bank employee, turns into an eccentric and maniacal green-skinned superhero who can bend
reality, after wearing a wooden mask that was created by Loki, the Norse god of mischief.

4
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Stanley Ipkiss / The Mask, played by Jim Carrey.

5
00:21:02,500 --> 00:21:08,500
Mitch Kellaway, played by Peter Riegert.

6
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:21,000
Dorian Tyrrell, played by Peter Greene.

7
00:29:27,500 --> 00:29:33,500
Peggy Brandt, played by Amy Yasbeck.

8
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:46,000
Charlie Schumaker, played by Richard Jeni.

9
00:37:52,500 --> 00:37:58,500
Niko, played by Orestes Matacena.

10
00:42:05,000 --> 00:42:11,000
The Mask is a 1994 American superhero slapstick film loosely based on the
1991 comic book series by John Arcudi and Doug Mahnke.

11
00:46:17,500 --> 00:46:23,500
Directed by Chuck Russell and written by Mike Werb, the film stars Jim Carrey, Peter
Riegert, Peter Greene, Amy Yasbeck, Richard Jeni and Cameron Diaz.

12
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:36,000
The plot follows Stanley Ipkiss (Carrey), a hapless and timid bank teller who finds an enchanted mask that transforms
him into a green-faced troublemaker who can cartoonishly alter himself and his surroundings at will.

13
00:54:42,500 --> 00:54:48,500
It is the first film in the Mask franchise.

14
00:58:55,000 --> 00:59:01,000
Principal photography began in Los Angeles on August
30, 1993, and concluded in October.

15
01:03:07,500 --> 01:03:13,500
The film marked the acting debut of Diaz, who was a model with no acting experience prior to filming, while Carrey, who was starring on the sketch
comedy series In Living Color and had just wrapped filming on Ace Ventura: Pet Detective (1994), was virtually unknown at the time.

16
01:07:20,000 --> 01:07:26,000
Their casting led to disputes from New Line Cinema executives who expressed concern that the film would be unsuccessful without
well-established actors, but the studio ultimately relented following reassurance from Russell that Carrey and Diaz were the right choices.

17
01:11:32,500 --> 01:11:38,500
The Mask was theatrically released in the United States
on July 29, 1994, to positive reviews.

18
01:15:45,000 --> 01:15:51,000
The film was a commercial success, grossing $352 million against its $18-23 million
production budget, becoming the fourth-highest-grossing film of 1994.

19
01:19:57,500 --> 01:20:03,500
It also influenced the resurgence of swing music in the 1990s.

20
01:24:10,000 --> 01:24:16,000
Carrey was nominated for Best Actor at the 52nd Golden Globe Awards and the film
was nominated for Best Visual Effects at the 67th Academy Awards.

21
01:28:22,500 --> 01:28:28,500
A sequel, Son of the Mask, was released in 2005.

22
01:32:35,000 --> 01:32:41,000
The film explores themes of dual identity, bank,
superhero, mockery, transformation.

23
01:36:47,500 --> 01:36:53,500
The tone is lighthearted and emotional and mind_bending.
